<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    What the look of a place does to mood (RimWorld: the Beauty ThoughtDef and ThoughtWorker_Beauty). Six
    stages, one per band of Need_Beauty.CurCategory that is not Neutral - a citizen in an unremarkable room
    carries no thought at all rather than a zero-offset one.

    This is the single mood consumer of the beauty need, and the route every ugly or beautiful thing takes to
    mood: filth reaches mood through here, by carrying a negative Beauty stat, the way RimWorld's does. The
    situational-thought handler finds any ThoughtDef with a worker by scanning, so this needed no edit to any
    shared file - a new worker class and this new file is the whole wiring (CLAUDE.md).

    It replaces Thoughts_Filth.xml's FilthyRoom thought, which read room cleanliness directly precisely
    because nothing implemented IEnvironmentSampler at the time, and whose own doc said to delete it the day
    one landed rather than let filth hurt mood twice. See the beauty module's report.

    The mood offsets are SimWorld's own - RimWorld's were not sourceable here - and BeautyTests pins that a
    worse environment is never a better mood, not these numbers.
  -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Beauty</defName>
    <workerClass>SimWorld.Needs.ThoughtWorker_NeedBeauty</workerClass>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>hideous environment</label>
        <description>Everywhere I look there is squalor.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-8</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>very ugly environment</label>
        <description>This place is genuinely unpleasant to be in.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-5</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>ugly environment</label>
        <description>This place could do with some care.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-3</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>pretty environment</label>
        <description>It is pleasant here.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>2</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>very pretty environment</label>
        <description>Somebody has made this place lovely.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>4</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>beautiful environment</label>
        <description>I could look at this all day.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>6</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
